  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-6 privacy-container">
          <div class="signup-container">
            <b>Not yet registered?</b>
            <a href="/signup"
              ><button class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Sign up</button></a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="login-container">
            <b>Already Registered?</b>
            <a href="/login"
              ><button class="btn btn-outline-success">Log in</button></a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-6">
          <h2>WanderLust Terms</h2>
          <br />
          <p>
            Please read these Terms of Service ("Terms") carefully before using
            the Wanderlust website, mobile application, or
            services(collectively, the "Platform"). By accessing or using the
            Platform, creating an account, or making a booking, you acknowledge
            that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms
            and our Privacy Policy. These Terms constitute the entire agreement
            between you and Wanderlust regarding the Platform and supersede all
            prior negotiations, representations, and agreements, whether written
            or oral
          </p>
          <h4>USER ELIGIBILITY AND RESTRICTIONS</h4>
          <p>
            You must be at least 18 years old and of legal age in your
            jurisdiction to use the Platform. By using the Platform, you
            represent and warrant that you have the legal capacity to enter into
            a binding contract. We do not knowingly permit anyone under 18 to
            register, and we will terminate accounts for users under 18.
          </p>
          <br />
          <h3>Account Restrictions</h3>
          <br />
          <p>
            We reserve the right to refuse service to anyone for any reason and
            at any time. We may restrict or terminate your account if we
            determine you pose a safety risk, have violated these Terms, or have
            engaged in fraudulent or illegal activity.You are responsible for
            maintaining the confidentiality of your password and username. You
            are fully responsible for all activities that occur under your
            account, whether or not you authorized them.
          </p>
          <br />
        </div>
        <div class="col-6">
          <h3>DAMAGE POLICIES AND LIABILITY</h3>
          <p>
            <b>Normal Wear and Tear:</b> Minor damage considered normal use
            (small marks on walls, worn furniture, slight stains on linens).
          </p>
          <br />
          <p>
            <b>Damages Beyond Normal Wear:</b> Host damage caused by guest
            negligence or violation of house rules (broken furniture, large
            stains, damage to appliances, broken windows, damaged doors).
          </p>
          <br />
          <h3>Damage Claims</h3>
          <p>
            Hosts may file damage claims within [14] days of checkout. Damage
            claims must include:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Photos of the damage</li>
            <li>Description of the damage and cause</li>
            <li>Repair or replacement cost estimate</li>
          </ul>
          <h4>WanderLust will:</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Review the claim and request guest comment if applicable</li>
            <li>Determine if damage exceeds normal wear and tear</li>
            <li>Assess if damage is guest's responsibility</li>
            <li>
              Deduct approved amount from guest's payment or charge guest's
              payment method
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Host Liability Insurance</h3>
          <p>
            Hosts are responsible for obtaining appropriate property insurance.
            Wanderlust is not responsible for property damage or loss.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12 offset-3">
          <h3>CODE OF CONDUCT AND PROHIBITED BEHAVIOR</h3>
        </div>
      </div>
      <br />
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-4">
          <p>
            <b>Harassment and Discrimination:</b> Engage in any form of
            harassment, bullying, threats, or discriminatory behavior based on
            race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, caste, sexual
            orientation, sex, gender, gender identity, disability, age, or any
            other protected characteristic.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Illegal Activity:</b> Use the Platform to advertise, facilitate,
            or engage in illegal activities, including but not limited to drug
            trafficking, human trafficking, prostitution, or sales of stolen
            goods or counterfeit items.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Fraud and Misrepresentation:</b> Provide false information,
            misrepresent yourself, impersonate another person, or create
            multiple accounts for fraudulent purposes.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Abusive Content:</b> Post, send, or display content that is
            hateful, violent, sexually explicit, or otherwise abusive.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Spam and Manipulation:</b> Send unsolicited or spam messages,
            post repetitive content, or artificially manipulate review scores,
            listings, or visibility.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Unauthorized Access:</b> Attempt to access areas of the Platform
            you are not authorized to access, circumvent security measures, or
            probe for vulnerabilities.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Intellectual Property Violation:</b> Infringe on copyrights,
            trademarks, patents, or other intellectual property rights of
            Wanderlust or other users.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-4">
          <p>
            <b>Hosts:</b> You guarantee that all information in your listings is
            accurate, complete, and truthful. Your property description, photos,
            amenities, availability, and pricing must match the actual
            accommodation. You cannot misrepresent the property type, location,
            capacity, or condition.
          </p>
          <p>
            <b>Guests:</b> You agree to provide accurate information about the
            number of guests, intended use of the property, and booking details.
            You may not misrepresent your purpose for booking.
          </p>

          <h4>Honest Reviews and Ratings</h4>
          <p>
            You agree to provide honest, accurate reviews based on your actual
            experience. You will not:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Post fake or fraudulent reviews</li>
            <li>Post reviews based on bookings you didn't complete</li>
            <li>Accept payment in exchange for positive reviews</li>
            <li>Post reviews of properties you've never actually visited</li>
            <li>
              Post malicious or false negative reviews to damage a user's
              reputation
            </li>
          </ul>
          <h3>Prohibited Communication</h3>
          <p>You will not:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Contact another user for any purpose outside of arranging a
              booking or resolving booking issues
            </li>
            <li>
              Encourage users to communicate or transact outside the Platform to
              avoid platform fees
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4">
          <h3>Host Responsibilities</h3>
          <p>
            Accuracy: Your listing description, photos, amenities list, and
            pricing must accurately reflect the property. You are responsible
            for keeping your calendar accurate and available dates up-to-date.
          </p>
          <p>
            Compliance: Your listing must comply with all applicable laws and
            regulations, including local zoning laws, rental regulations,
            occupancy limits, and tax requirements.
          </p>
          <p>
            Condition and Cleanliness: You must provide the property in the
            condition described and ensure it is clean and well-maintained. You
            are responsible for any maintenance or repair issues.
          </p>
          <p>
            House Rules: You may establish reasonable house rules including:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Quiet hours</li>
            <li>Pet policies</li>
            <li>Smoking policies</li>
            <li>Guest capacity limits</li>
            <li>Parking requirements</li>
            <li>Check-in and check-out times</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Safety and Legality: You must:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Maintain working locks, security systems, and safety equipment
            </li>
            <li>Comply with building codes and safety regulations</li>
            <li>Provide accurate information about any safety hazards</li>
            <li>Maintain appropriate insurance coverage</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="route-listing">
